From c05a3a10425221ef3aa129526db53cc079907065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mjb-is <mjb-is@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:10:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 089/120] machinebackup: send the notification e-mail

proxmoxbackup-machine accepts the -mail-* options and the config file's
smtp section, and checks them in Config.Valid, but never sends anything.
It now sends the notification after the backup, for a failed run too,
the way proxmoxbackup-directory does: subject and body from
-mail-subject-template / -mail-body-template (or the config file), with
the default template when a custom one does not work, to every
configured recipient.

- The default templates move from machinebackuplib, where nothing used
  them, to machinebackup/main.go, as in directorybackup. The body leaves
  out the chunk counts, which machinebackuplib.Backup does not report.
- A mail that cannot be sent makes the run exit 1, as in
  directorybackup, but the backup's own error is still printed first.

Tests: a small fake SMTP server in machinebackup/main_test.go. One test
runs main() with a backup that fails before connecting to PBS and
checks that one "Backup Failed" mail arrives with the error in the
body; it fails on the unchanged code (0 mails). Two more call sendMail
directly for a successful run (two recipients) and for custom
templates. A live one (skipped unless PBS_LIVE_URL and the other
PBS_LIVE_* variables are set) backs up a small file as the device and
checks for one "Backup Success" mail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSSBMF6hRk92jsHCMKgDRx

Fork adaptation: machinebackuplib keeps the fork's var block. It already
had no mail templates; errUploadAborted is declared in windows.go there,
and didxMagic is unused, so upstream's side would have redeclared one and
added the other.

